---
import SectionHeader from "./SectionHeader.astro";
---

<section
	id="approach"
	class="border-b border-neutral-200/80 bg-white"
	aria-labelledby="approach-heading"
	style={`padding-top: var(--spacing-section-y); padding-bottom: var(--spacing-section-y);`}
>
	<div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6 lg:px-8">
		<div class="grid items-center gap-14 lg:grid-cols-2 lg:gap-20">
			<div class="flex flex-col gap-8">
				<SectionHeader
					label="Approach"
					title="Presence as the foundation of good therapy"
					titleId="approach-heading"
					class="mb-6! md:mb-8!"
				/>
				<div class="max-w-xl space-y-5 text-base leading-relaxed text-neutral-600 md:text-lg">
					<p>
						We were both moved by the Zulu greeting Sawbona, which means, &quot;I see you, I hear you,
						I feel you.&quot; It is a deep way of acknowledging a person&apos;s presence and a
						recognition of their worth, dignity, and value.
					</p>
					<p>
						This so aptly captures some of our aims. Of course, what we can guarantee is to be
						present, and so we settled on the word Ngikhona, which means &quot;I am here.&quot;
					</p>
					<p>
						Placeholder paragraph: here you might describe how sessions are structured, what
						confidentiality means in practice, or how you think about pace, endings, and
						collaboration. Keep the tone steady and informative rather than promotional.
					</p>
				</div>
			</div>
			<div class="relative flex aspect-4/3 min-h-[220px] w-full flex-col justify-end overflow-hidden rounded-sm border border-neutral-200/80 bg-accent p-8 lg:aspect-auto lg:min-h-[280px]">
				<p class="max-w-sm text-sm leading-relaxed text-neutral-900/85">
					Accent panel placeholder: a photograph, texture, or short line of copy can sit here. Use this
					area sparingly so the page stays calm.
				</p>
			</div>
		</div>
	</div>
</section>
